  "authentication_contract": "Only graph identity-context GET changes to Bearer graph:read and authenticated tenant intersection. Exact tenant predicates apply to Identity/Employee/Department/manager; global reference labels grant no exemption. Dedicated A/B keys, no shared-token fallback. Prior eight reader identities/env/mounts/files/scopes preserved.",
  "connection_contract": "New dedicated config file and request-local READ_ACCESS driver; closes on success/error without global initialization, retries or schema. API AISOC_DISABLE_NEO4J remains true. Shared Neo4j5.15 Community credential is privileged; session/query/API restrictions are not database-enforced read-only or tenant roles. Existing Bolt transport unchanged.",
  "query_contract": "Account-bounded distinct node paths; classify native ZONED DATETIME and filter before deterministic account/provider/node ordering and limit. Counts cover all matched paths for requested accounts: candidate=eligible+late+unverifiable, eligible=returned+truncated. Retain identities without linked employees and multi-provider/multi-employee ambiguity; bool false remains false, nonboolean active means unknown.",
  "cutoff_contract": "Known late native import stamps and all missing/unsupported stamps are rejected frozen, tightening the former partial allowance. Live may return unknown import stamps. Every served row remains without_timestamp for business history; adopted_without_timestamp counts actual subset. Employee import cutoff does not reconstruct later-edited department/manager/identity/edge history.",
  "projection_hash_contract": "Canonical scoped tenant plus24 normalized current path fields (source node IDs/kinds, provider/account, display attributes, linkage, relationship types, native UTC import/status/rawstamp hash). Not a complete database row, historical version or authentication signature.",
  "adoption_contract": "Typed request/cache/HTTP/graph source/counts, URL+credential+query+cutoff cache, mapping before cache; no stale failed-refresh adoption. Default300seconds cannot instantly observe server revocation/expiry or graph edits. Top5/field120/employment-end40 and complete3000-character block including advisory retained, exactly sanitized once; source projection and actual display/rendered/block hashes distinct.",
  "persistence_contract": "identity_context_read accompanies first-write verdict and independent artifact in the existing transaction. Failure rolls back, retry does not duplicate; generic Run/alert retry semantics unchanged. No new schema or model scoring.",
  "fixture_contract": "27 marked synthetic nodes/22 relations in existing A/B tenants; original shared graph empty, no schema migration. Two separately named history properties may be changed to show import-time partiality; only exact marked objects changed. Read fixture is not HR sync, directory import/authoring or real authorization proof. Model uses natural new account/rule without MITRE, old skills/KB/dispositions no_match; all four prior readers separately checked by original queries.",
  "failure_contract": "Actual dedicated-config removal causes HTTP503 graph_not_configured and production worker/prompt projection, with finally byte/permission restoration; shared graph remains running. Actual Neo4j query error/recovery in a probe session is distinct from HTTP503 and shared outage. Real PG artifact fault is probe-only, never a second model.",
  "scope_limitations": [
    "Only A/B test tenants configured; shared privileged graph credential and clear Bolt are not full production isolation/transport security.",
    "No HR business-effective history exists; all adopted identity paths remain historically unverified.",
    "One model example does not accept full classification/calibration or investigation quality. Resident worker/graph/approvals/real responses remain disabled."
  ]
}
